skill: "fx-hedging-advisor"
sections[3]:
  - "# fx-hedging-advisor\n\nNet currency exposures and draft a hedging recommendation inside policy bands. Use when invoicing or spending is concentrated in a currency other than the functional one, when the treasury policy review comes up, or before any forward contract or option is quoted. Outputs a decision memo; it never executes a hedge itself.\n\nOwner: role-treasury-banking-spec (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"invoice ledger export by currency; expense forecast by currency from cashflow-13w.toon; treasury policy treasury-policy.toon with per-pair hedge bands; existing hedge register fx-hedge-register.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/fx-exposure-register.toon with net exposure per pair; agents/artifacts/finance/hedge-memo.toon with recommended ratio, instrument, tenor and an approval block\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load the invoice ledger and the expense forecast; group both by currency pair against the functional currency.\n2. Net inflows against outflows per pair per month; record gross, offset and residual in the exposure register.\n3. Subtract existing hedges recorded in fx-hedge-register.toon (mark-to-value by remaining tenor) from each residual.\n4. Compare the hedged share against the policy band for that pair; classify as under-hedged, in-band or over-hedged.\n5. Fetch indicative spot and forward rates with search_web and label every rate as indicative and timestamped; recompute exposure at those rates with run_command.\n6. Draft the hedge memo only for pairs classified under-hedged beyond the policy tolerance; state the recommended instrument (forward default, option where cash-flow timing is uncertain), notional and tenor.\n7. Attach the arithmetic: notional, floor share, band edges and resulting worst-case unhedged loss at a 10 percent adverse move.\n8. Emit ask_question to role-cfo with the memo for the R3 approval; do not send instructions to any broker or bank.\n9. On approval, append the decision to fx-hedge-register.toon and mark the memo executed-pending-settlement; settlement confirmation is reconciled by settlement-reconciliation-audit.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nmemo to role-cfo for R3 approval; settlement flows audited by settlement-reconciliation-audit.\n"
